course: dictionary
lesson: 15592
title: Tabulate: putting information in a table
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words come from maths and science lessons. Tabulate is one of them. It means to arrange information in a table, in rows and columns, so that it is easy to read and compare.
explain: Imagine a class measuring how far a toy car rolls on carpet, wood and tiles. «We tabulated the results in a table with three columns.» The clue is the word table, which sits inside tabulate. Each time you read the word, ask: would it make sense to put this information into rows and columns?
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «We put the results into a table» means the same as «We tabulated the results», so your meaning fits. Then you can understand the word even if you have never used it before.
fact: Tabulate means to arrange information in a table, in rows and columns.
fact: Tabulate is a verb: tabulate, tabulates, tabulated, tabulating.
fact: «Tabulate the results» means put the results into a table.
fact: Data is information collected from an experiment or a survey.
fact: Scientists usually tabulate their data before they draw a graph.
exercise: «Ravi tabulated the results of his experiment.» What does tabulated mean? | Thrown away | *Arranged in a table | Drawn as a picture of a tree | Read out loud to the class
exercise: «Please tabulate the data from our survey before we draw the graph.» What should you do first? | Forget the data | *Put the data into a table | Write a poem about the survey | Draw the graph
exercise: Find and copy the word that means to arrange information in a table. | graph | survey | *tabulate | results
test: «The children tabulated how many pets each person had.» What does tabulated mean here? | Lost on the way home | Counted in their heads and forgot | *Put into rows and columns | Sang a song about pets
test: Which phrase means put the results into a table? | Hide the survey | *Tabulate the results | Graph the poem | Ignore the data
exam: Maya asks, "Why do scientists tabulate their results?" What is the best answer? | *So the results are easy to read and compare | So the results can be hidden from everyone | So they can forget what they found | So the results can be sung like a song
